Subject: [PATCH 2/2] src/lab-process-mail: Quarantine mail from unapproved
 senders
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: xosoprrqnznooqywkkvoskqskltlvzpk
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:05:29 +0000

The list takes posts from anyone who can reach lab-mail, and every
inbox message becomes an agent pass that may change code and push it.
Mail is untrusted input, so a stranger's message must never be what
drives the agent, however it reached the list.

The check runs in the loop, before the agent sees anything, so it does
not depend on what a model decides. A message whose From is not one
listed address is moved into the list's quarantine/ maildir instead,
and the move is pushed on the outbox like a reply, so it leaves the
inbox for every reader and the loop goes on. Moving the file back
releases it. With no list of senders the loop refuses to start rather
than trust everyone.
